    {
      "id": "9oUSug3y_8MAGf9HE8URt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2029.5833333333326,
      "y": -1058.7976190476202,
      "width": 1497.714680989583,
      "height": 531.6666666666655,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 987162158,
      "version": 1212,
      "versionNonce": 1397950443,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779604680409,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "According to formula we have Qx = (4, 128) and Kx = (4,128) we can't multiply\nthese to mat mul we need column\nof first value is equal to rows of second values but here we have 128 != 4 so\nwe take transpose of kx then divide with embeddings let's take an example :\nso we got Qx.kx = (4,128).(128,4) we got (4,4) size matrix in return that we\ndivide with total emb and multi with (4,4).(4,128) and the answer i get in shape\n(4, 128) that is called attention.\n\nNow we shape :\n\n",
      "fontSize": 38.666666666666586,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "According to formula we have Qx = (4, 128) and Kx = (4,128) we can't multiply these to mat mul we need column\nof first value is equal to rows of second values but here we have 128 != 4 so we take transpose of kx then divide with embeddings let's take an example :\nso we got Qx.kx = (4,128).(128,4) we got (4,4) size matrix in return that we divide with total emb and multi with (4,4).(4,128) and the answer i get in shape \n(4, 128) that is called attention.\n\nNow we shape :\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "kkith9ven3OK87gSKhzDM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3590.416666666665,
      "y": -1618.79761904762,
      "width": 1649.42822265625,
      "height": 870.0000000000005,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b20",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1067702066,
      "version": 1304,
      "versionNonce": 979637605,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779604693320,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is K, Q and V :\nIn transformer model we the attention layer that find the sematic meaning\nof the words to make sense like there is a word apple without these attention \nkey , query and value the apple can be anything the company and fruit so there\nis ambigous so in attention we have key query and value.\n\nQuery : it is like a question asking what am i looking for ? e.g in the example \nthe sky is blue ? we take the blue in example the blue is like a query it is asking for \nits key so it ask prevous words what is my key and value like where am i belong to!\n\nKey : Its like all the prevous values that query is looking for first it go for the it has\nlet's say 'the' score is 0.4 , sky score is 0.8, and for is is 0.38. So the highest score is\n0.8 and it is its key.\n\nValue: Now we have the key which is 0.8 and its value is 'sky' so we key value become \nsky-blue. \n\n",
      "fontSize": 38.666666666666686,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is K, Q and V :\nIn transformer model we the attention layer that find the sematic meaning\nof the words to make sense like there is a word apple without these attention \nkey , query and value the apple can be anything the company and fruit so there\nis ambigous so in attention we have key query and value.\n\nQuery : it is like a question asking what am i looking for ? e.g in the example \nthe sky is blue ? we take the blue in example the blue is like a query it is asking for \nits key so it ask prevous words what is my key and value like where am i belong to!\n\nKey : Its like all the prevous values that query is looking for first it go for the it has\nlet's say 'the' score is 0.4 , sky score is 0.8, and for is is 0.38. So the highest score is\n0.8 and it is its key.\n\nValue: Now we have the key which is 0.8 and its value is 'sky' so we key value become \nsky-blue. \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
