      "text": "The SwiGLU FFN",
      "fontSize": 51.99999999999999,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The SwiGLU FFN",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "60kspRydKisRONGJMJjmZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2043.943658541301,
      "y": 247.86241104875637,
      "width": 1835.50927734375,
      "height": 459.99999999999955,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 291417221,
      "version": 520,
      "versionNonce": 1180981387,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779605914503,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In next stage The SwiGLU FFN :\n\nwe take three matrices gate_proj , up_proj , and down_proj \nx1 = gate_proj(tensor) = (4, 512)\nx2 = up_proj(tensor) = Output shape is (4, 512)\nNow we take x1 and run it through the SilU (Swish) activation function.What does Swish do? It acts \nlike a smart gate filter. \nIf a number is negative or useless, it turns it into 0. If it's positive and important, it lets it pass.\nThen, we multiply the filtered x1 directly by x2 :\n    Combined = {SiLU}(x1) x (x2)",
      "fontSize": 36.79999999999997,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In next stage The SwiGLU FFN :\n\nwe take three matrices gate_proj , up_proj , and down_proj \nx1 = gate_proj(tensor) = (4, 512)\nx2 = up_proj(tensor) = Output shape is (4, 512)\nNow we take x1 and run it through the SilU (Swish) activation function.What does Swish do? It acts \nlike a smart gate filter. \nIf a number is negative or useless, it turns it into 0. If it's positive and important, it lets it pass.\nThen, we multiply the filtered x1 directly by x2 :\n    Combined = {SiLU}(x1) x (x2)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
